  "findings": [
    "Batching cut the recruiter prompt from 77-95 KB to 53 KB, 47 KB and 25 KB for the three batches of a five-unit plan (typed recall 20, 15 and 7 KB; 49, 53 and 24 detail cards).",
    "It did not lower the per-call failure rate: 7 of 12 batch calls were rejected on their first reply (candidate row shape, negative-evidence shape, units object shape, invalid ranking, omitted units) against 2 of 2 single calls, so a batched turn spent 3 to 6 recruiter calls where the single call spent 2.",
    "Every rejected batch reply was repaired within its batch and the whole team assembled and verified once; two of the four batched turns were then vetoed by the strict critic (wrong-neighbour pointers on the discovery unit), which the single-call turns did not meet in two samples.",
    "The reply failures are reply-shape failures of the serving deployment, not omissions under prompt size; the smallest batch (25 KB) failed its first reply in two of four samples."
  ],
  "limits": "Small samples; no controlled A/B beyond the same wording on the same day; the critic vetoes are single judgements on stochastic teams."
}
